 "policy_profile": "t24-mysql-resource-group",
 "description": "T24 MySQL CPU resource-group lifecycle (issue #103, R2 verdict): CREATE/ALTER/DROP RESOURCE GROUP reach kind=ddl with audited semantics under MySQL — a dedicated MySQLResourceGroupDeclaration (TYPE required first on CREATE, positional VCPU / THREAD_PRIORITY / ENABLE|DISABLE slots, FORCE trailing on ALTER/DROP) kept strictly separate from the TiDB RU declaration. The version premise is the 8.0.3 introduction boundary (a proven pre-8.0.3 version refuses every lifecycle statement before any catalog read; an unproven version owes unknown_resource_group_version) and the deployment feature/capability/privilege/host-vcpu/occupancy facts are independent premise facts — each unproven one owes its bounded evidence gap, never a guessed default. Reserved usr_default/sys_default refuse ALTER/DROP case-insensitively by name alone. An inverted declared VCPU range is a declaration-provable semantic refusal (ER_INVALID_VCPU_RANGE), never a parse failure; ALTER FORCE without DISABLE is equally declaration-provable. THREAD_PRIORITY bounds are capability-gated (capability on: SYSTEM -20..0 / USER 0..19 refuses; off: an authored nonzero is ignored with the effective value storing zero; unknown: bounded gap plus withheld member). DROP without FORCE on a proven-occupied group refuses (ER_RESOURCE_GROUP_BUSY); an unproven occupancy owes unknown_resource_group_occupancy. Every premise fact unproven keeps the outcome undecidable — success notices and post-state publication suppress, post-state members diverging between proceeding branches stay withheld. Bare DROP RESOURCE GROUP <name> binds the MySQL registry under MySQL; the MySQL CPU forms under TiDB and the TiDB RU forms under MySQL stay vendor boundaries; SET RESOURCE GROUP ... FOR is a bounded unaudited feature under MySQL and a vendor boundary under TiDB. metadata_cases encode native probes — none has run and none may be claimed as native PASS.",
